buckets.test.ts: hoist the test account out of beforeEach.

`userCreated` gates signup so the account is created exactly once per worker
process, but `email` was generated fresh on every beforeEach invocation. The
first test in a worker signed up and logged in fine; every subsequent test in
that same worker called loginByCreds() with a brand-new UUID address that had
never been registered.

loginByCreds() does not assert that login succeeded, so the run stayed on
/login and the next call, navigationMenu.switchPassphrase(), blocked on
PROJECT_SELECT_XPATH until the 30s test timeout fired inside the hook:

    Test timeout of 30000ms exceeded while running "beforeEach" hook.
    waiting for locator('//div[div[div[text()='Project']]]')

Retries start a fresh worker, so userCreated is false again and the retry
passes -- the failures surface as "flaky" rather than "failed".

Every other test file in tests/default already scopes email to the describe
closure; buckets.test.ts was the outlier.

